                <pb facs="0171" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg65"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Wilson to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 8,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Watson, commissioner emigration South Carolina, has made formal application
                    Belgian Government to be permitted to advance passage money Belgian emigrants;
                    advances made by State to be repaid by emigrants. Watson states in application
                    that this method has approval of Sargent and Government, and has asked me to
                    exert influence with foreign office here. This have refused to do without
                    express instructions from the department. A hurry answer is requested, as 500
                    emigrants are ready to sail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
